from mkchar import write
write("Vesta_Carmis_Zell","Vesta Carmis Zell","3 (astral king); 2 for her messengers","9","13","Books 9, 10 (chapter files); notes for Books 11-13","Jes_Fin_Kaal.md, Marek_Nior_Vargas.md, Tera_Jun_Casta.md, ../02_Cosmology_and_Powers/Astral_Kings_and_Messengers.md",
 "The astral king who rules the messenger forces around Yaresh and keeps her servants capped with seals.",
 "- Jason is told she is \"the astral king who rules the local messenger forces\" and a known practitioner of soul engineering (Book 9, Ch78 L82).\n- She watches servant race armies battle to the death, resurrecting them and bestowing abilities \"to keep things interesting\" (Book 9, Ch102 L65); she feels one of her seals vanish when Jason removes it from Tera (Book 9, Ch102 L66-67).\n- Marek served her until recently; she was known for her fascination with soul engineering (Book 10, Ch1 L53). Jason removes the brand of \"her astral king master, Vesta Carmis Zell\" from Tera Jun Casta (Book 10, Ch2 L19) and says Vesta used Tera, keeping her at silver rank (Book 10, Ch2 L40).\n- At the Council of Kings her prime avatar scolds Jamis (Book 10, Ch15 L8); he says she chose a separate goal from the rest of the group and is young (Book 10, Ch15 L30-43).\n- Boris says she hired messengers with elemental powers and would never accept a member of the Unorthodoxy, and has no idea he is one (Book 11, Ch24 L85-86).",
 "Cold, curious and acquisitive; she treats the lives of her servants as experiments.")
write("Jes_Fin_Kaal","Jes Fin Kaal","2","9","11","Books 9, 10, 11 (chapter files)","Vesta_Carmis_Zell.md, Benella.md, Fal_Vin_Garath.md",
 "A gold-rank messenger ritualist and Voice of the Will who leads the messengers' dealings with Yaresh.",
 "- A messenger ritualist new to the stronghold, \"referred to by the other messengers as Voice Kaal\" (Book 9, Ch55 L19); she is smaller than the others, barely over seven feet, and Benella cannot magically detect her although she is gold rank (Book 9, Ch55 L27).\n- She wears a loose deep-red robe with white trim and pristine white wings (Book 9, Ch55 L28) and says \"I am Voice Kaal, and you may address me as such\" (Book 9, Ch56 L14).\n- She probes Benella's emotions with her aura to learn why she brought Jason to the messengers' attention (Book 9, Ch56 L22-26).\n- In Book 10 she is the messengers' leadership at Yaresh, a Voice of the Will (Book 10, Ch9 L49); Jason says she has played things mostly straight but kept things from them (Book 10, Ch59 L38).\n- Boris says she believed Destruction wanted a massive explosion once the messengers claimed the soul forge (Book 10, Ch81 L36).",
 "Quiet, exact and unreadable; she lets others speak and listens for what they leave out.")
write("Fal_Vin_Garath","Fal Vin Garath","2","9","9","Book 9 (chapter files)","Jes_Fin_Kaal.md, Benella.md, Familiars.md",
 "A silver-rank messenger master who is abusive but within the bounds his peers accept.",
 "- \"Fal Vin Garath was Benella's master, who was abusive but not outside the bounds of acceptability to his fellow messengers\", free to treat the servant races as he pleased so long as it did not impinge on other messengers (Book 9, Ch56 L5).\n- He has fair skin and golden hair, a physical counterpart to the other silver messenger (Book 9, Ch56 L5-7).\n- He scowls at Benella and demands answers in a voice \"like a command from the heavens\" (Book 9, Ch52 L20-28).\n- He launches a soul attack on Jason through his connection to Shade, and is surprised when Jason fends it off and retaliates (Book 9, Ch52 L36).\n- He seizes Shade and squeezes while Shade drains his mana, until Shade's body is destroyed (Book 9, Ch52 L42-44).",
 "Imperious and quick to anger; he assumes servants exist to answer him.")
write("Benella","Benella","2","9","9","Book 9 (chapter files)","Jes_Fin_Kaal.md, Fal_Vin_Garath.md, Jason_Asano.md",
 "A servant of the messengers who works as Zolit's aide and brings Jason to their attention.",
 "- She corrects someone who mispronounces her name (Book 9, Ch46 L40) and offers Jason fight outfits from her duffel (Book 9, Ch46 L44).\n- She is Zolit's quiet aide at the fights (Book 9, Ch47 L25, L49).\n- Her master is Fal Vin Garath (Book 9, Ch56 L5); he scolds her and demands she explain the servant races' different way (Book 9, Ch52 L20-29).\n- She has \"one chance to prove herself still valuable to the messengers\" by presenting Jason Asano as a potential threat (Book 9, Ch56 L4), and presents the issue to Voice Kaal personally (Book 9, Ch56 L20).\n- Kaal probes her emotions and deduces there is more to it than she says (Book 9, Ch56 L22-26).",
 "Careful, watchful and afraid; she hides what she thinks behind a servant's neutrality.")
write("Kasper_Irios","Kasper Irios","0","7","9","Books 7, 9 (chapter files)","Zara_Rimaros.md, ../05_Organisations/Guilds_and_Houses.md",
 "A peak-bronze heir of House Irios whom Jason meets after the Zara marriage scandal.",
 "- Jason meets him at a tailor's shop: \"a peak-level bronze-ranker\" (Book 7, Ch41 L3); he is shocked when Jason names himself the dead man (Book 7, Ch41 L11-12).\n- Jason walks him along the street and locals glance at the House Irios crest on his arm (Book 7, Ch41 L26); a trio of young bronze-ranker friends greet him (Book 7, Ch41 L40-41).\n- Zara's intended match was \"a member of the Irios family\" (Book 7, Ch18 L70), which is why the encounter is political.\n- In Book 9 Jason's overture to the Irios family was not taken up, and Vesper had engineered the meeting for political reasons (Book 9, Ch14 L11).",
 "Shaken and eager to please; he is caught between his family's pride and Jason's reputation.")
write("Jota_Withers","Jota Withers","3","12","13","Books 12, 13 (chapter files)","Anna_Tilden.md, ../06_Places/Astral_Spaces/00_Astral_Overview.md",
 "A gold-rank dimension ship captain in a pirate admiral's service who is sent to Earth in Book 12.",
 "- He sits on the bridge of his dimension ship, reflecting that the universe-city of Interstice is \"for most practical purposes, the centre of the cosmos\" (Book 12, Ch57 L3).\n- Born in a feeder realm, he fell short of Interstice at gold rank; arrogance cost him opportunities and he ended up serving \"a self-styled cosmic admiral\" who was a pirate lord (Book 12, Ch57 L7-12).\n- His vessel is a rarity, only gold rank, which suits certain jobs (Book 12, Ch57 L14).\n- On Earth he is hosted by the Asano clan matriarch Noriko, who visits daily (Book 12, Ch63 L16-19).\n- He watches Jason float towards him, noting his impenetrable aura and the scars that are probably not affectations (Book 12, Ch64 L76-79).",
 "Weary, proud and cautious; a gold-ranker who has always been one rung short of what he was promised.")
write("Argy","Argy (Emmett Dillivan)","0","7","8","Books 7, 8 (chapter files)","Pelli.md, ../06_Places/Rimaros.md",
 "A fruit grower in Palisaros who calls himself Argy and brings Jason to the mayor.",
 "- \"Emmett Dillivan, but folks just call me Argy\", after the fruit he is eating, which looks like a large tangerine (Book 7, Ch13 L18-20).\n- His family has grown the fruit \"longer than most can remember\" (Book 7, Ch13 L20).\n- He tells Jason to talk to Pelli and offers to take him (Book 7, Ch13 L28).\n- Jason calls the place \"a genuine paradise\" (Book 7, Ch13 L24).",
 "Easygoing and proud of his town; he treats visitors as guests until they give a reason not to.")
write("Pelli","Pelli","0","7","8","Books 7, 8 (chapter files)","Argy.md, Liara_Rimaros.md, ../06_Places/Rimaros.md",
 "The sharp-tongued mayor of Palisaros and a contact for Jason in the Storm Kingdom.",
 "- Argy tells Jason \"You'll want to talk to Pelli\" (Book 7, Ch13 L28); she insists \"The name's Pelli and I'll thank you to use it\" (Book 7, Ch13 L51).\n- She asks Rufus how his father took him being a magic swordsman (Book 7, Ch13 L51).\n- She is the mayor of Palisaros (Book 7, Ch13 L28-30).\n- She asks Jason whether Soramir should have told him something (Book 7, Ch18 L43).",
 "Blunt and watchful; she protects the town's quiet life from outsiders.")
